+	 *
+	 * It binds `(init-program)` and `(go)` with bind_func, which is `is-cfunc`
+	 * (libopenbios/clib.fs:17), which is `$create` -- and $create defines into
+	 * the CURRENT vocabulary. While a device context is open, the words land in
+	 * that node instead of the dictionary, where $find cannot see them.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on x86 BEFORE this move: `(init-program)` MISSING, `(go)`
+	 * MISSING, `platform-boot` (bound just below device_end) FOUND. The symptom
+	 * was `load` of any file ending in "Unable to locate (init-program)!"
+	 * (forth/debugging/client.fs:57), so the whole `load` client path was dead
+	 * on the arch that has had CONFIG_LOADER_FORTH set to true all along.
+	 *
+	 * NOTE what is deliberately NOT moved: the cif-claim/cif-release binds a few
+	 * lines above are wrapped in find-device /openprom/client-services ...
+	 * device_end() ON PURPOSE. Those are NODE METHODS -- ppc and sparc install
+	 * the same two names via NODE_METHODS on that same node -- so their being
+	 * invisible to a global $find is correct, not a second instance of this bug.
+	 * That distinction was checked before touching anything. */
+	openbios_init();
+
